{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X\\ge 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 2) & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{\\infty }{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{2}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1353\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424001 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423998 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424001 1069 "q-96345" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424001 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424001 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{4}),$ calculate $P(X<1).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424001 1072 #uuid "24af5ca9-8d38-530b-8002-d4db8feaa5d7" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424001 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{4}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-3x/4}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(X<1)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{-3x/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3x/4}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-3/4}+{e}^{0} \\\\  & ≈0.5276\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424002 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423997 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424002 1069 "q-96417" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424002 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424002 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424002 1072 #uuid "548f5527-3c2c-5249-846d-012dddb74912" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424002 1074 "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(1\\le X\\le 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2x}{|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-6}+{e}^{-2} \\\\  & ≈0.1329\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424003 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423996 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424003 1069 "q-253929" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424003 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424003 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X>6\\,|\\,X>4).$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424003 1072 #uuid "840fc6bd-43f7-5e1f-9678-e0daa00596e7" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424003 1074 "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the momeryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=6.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=6-4=2\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6\\,|\\,X>4) & ={e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & ={e}^{-(2)\\cdot (2)} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424004 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423995 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424004 1069 "q-96407" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424004 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424004 1071 "Given that the random variable $U∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(U\\ge 3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424004 1072 #uuid "9e3c60ce-47c9-5c4f-b8dd-973c8222fab3" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424004 1074 "An exponential random variable $U$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nU∼\\text{Exp}(2).\n$$\n\nSo, $U$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-2u}, & u\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(U\\ge 3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U\\ge 3) & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-2u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2u}{|}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-6} \\\\  & ≈0.0025\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424005 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423999 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424005 1069 "q-253938" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424005 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424005 1071 "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>6).$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424005 1072 #uuid "b6017236-d9af-57fe-9a24-c8e569cb2642" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true] [17592186424005 1074 "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =2,$ $s=6,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-6=3\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>6) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(2)\\cdot (3)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534516 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00532a77-8369-5069-a645-da39692238cd" 17592186423964 "answer-09a50814-795d-5d28-8e92-209754c2af10" 17592186423965 "answer-20637901-6ccf-5b0b-8845-93cfcc926093" 17592186423966 "answer-2a753c6c-3899-5081-81c1-9c51956a63b5" 17592186423967 "answer-2c1745b6-630b-529f-9136-c40f62c94d25" 17592186423968 "answer-31d5edd8-2b29-5eba-8a70-917a5b0f20f3" 17592186423969 "answer-39d93c58-7d48-5de8-9930-8560bb4ab222" 17592186423970 "answer-3b8a2e77-056b-5c7d-a4a5-f0b85875f98a" 17592186423971 "answer-3f517b2d-d281-5139-846d-3d24808ad7b5" 17592186423972 "answer-4d1edc2d-b633-52ba-85a7-13aec31489a3" 17592186423973 "answer-4e91c1c2-03b1-5f7b-accf-22d6915d4b08" 17592186423974 "answer-5ba4d575-3c96-585c-87ae-967c1404dc69" 17592186423975 "answer-6cf46d04-45a1-535e-a92e-c9cb35404ba7" 17592186423976 "answer-6fadb770-777f-5d25-8c8e-520eb1a7bac1" 17592186423977 "answer-71609beb-d000-5d09-b83b-5c7ae828643f" 17592186423978 "answer-78e06ba4-70f9-51bf-9980-6444eb5316e8" 17592186423979 "answer-7c7853be-90ec-5040-a947-22a3b32a3ad5" 17592186423980 "answer-950530ce-1ae8-509e-b4cd-ed8ae399b36c" 17592186423981 "answer-95ffeb01-adda-57d6-881e-fcb39a8b7a3c" 17592186423982 "answer-9ef5aef2-1def-50a9-8422-76dce776ddf1" 17592186423983 "answer-a4655f58-d989-5a50-8b84-0a0259d6d8f3" 17592186423984 "answer-a59b312d-c446-5a83-97bf-18385fce9ef9" 17592186423985 "answer-b5df255f-d5f8-5d26-a865-2d00936b6ac3" 17592186423986 "answer-bd231bf4-aff5-5dd1-9238-2de